{"id":"lot","name":"Lot","aliases":["Lot, The","Lot"],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:lot","nave:lot-the"],"groups":["2. The son of Haran","Accompanies Abraham to Egypt","Rich in flocks, and herds, and servants"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Lot","text":"(Heb. goral, a “pebble”), a small stone used in casting lots (Num. 33:54; Jonah 1:7). The lot was always resorted to by the Hebrews with strictest reference to the interposition of God, and as a method of ascertaining the divine will (Prov. 16:33), and in serious cases of doubt (Esther 3:7). Thus the lot was used at the division of the land of Canaan among the serveral tribes (Num. 26:55; 34:13), at the detection of Achan (Josh. 7:14, 18), the election of Saul to be king (1 Sam. 10:20, 21), the distribution of the priestly offices of the temple service (1 Chr. 24:3, 5, 19; Luke 1:9), and over the two goats at the feast of Atonement (Lev. 16:8). Matthias, who was “numbered with the eleven” (Acts 1:24-26), was chosen by lot. This word also denotes a portion or an inheritance (Josh. 15:1; Ps. 125:3; Isa. 17:4), and a destiny, as assigned by God (Ps. 16:5; Dan. 12:13). Lot, (Heb. lot), a …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H1486","lemma":"גּוֹרָל","xlit":"gôwrâl","gloss":"a pebble","kjv":"lot","count":23,"share":0.19},{"strong":"H3876","lemma":"לוֹט","xlit":"Lôwṭ","gloss":"Lot, Abraham's nephew","kjv":"Lot","count":15,"share":0.13},{"strong":"H87","lemma":"אַבְרָם","xlit":"ʼAbrâm","gloss":"Abram, the original name of Abraham","kjv":"Abram","count":12,"share":0.1},{"strong":"H5307","lemma":"נָפַל","xlit":"nâphal","gloss":"to fall, in a great variety of applications","kjv":"be accepted, cast, out), cease","count":14,"share":0.12},{"strong":"H5467","lemma":"סְדֹם","xlit":"Çᵉdôm","gloss":"Sedom, a place near the Dead Sea","kjv":"Sodom","count":8,"share":0.07},{"strong":"H3920","lemma":"לָכַד","xlit":"lâkad","gloss":"to catch","kjv":"at all, catch, be frozen, be holden","count":9,"share":0.08}],"verses":["Lev.16.